{
  "id": "ep090",
  "duration": 45.257,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.455,
      "text": "A crashed space probe fell silent, yet spoke from Venus weeks later.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "1972 CPA 4166.jpg",
        "credit": "USSR Post",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1972_CPA_4166.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.455,
      "end": 10.575,
      "text": "On December 15, 1970, the Soviet Union reached the dark night side of Venus.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.467,
          "end": 10.567,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 10.575,
      "end": 17.295,
      "text": "Engineers built Venera 7 inside a thick titanium pressure shell to survive the extreme heat.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Cut-away model of a Soviet Venera 12 lander.jpg",
        "credit": "Don S. Montgomery, U.S. Navy (Ret.)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cut-away_model_of_a_Soviet_Venera_12_lander.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 10.567,
          "end": 13.567,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 13.567,
          "end": 17.3,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.295,
      "end": 23.065,
      "text": "During descent, the parachute failed, causing the heavy spacecraft to slam into the ground.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Space probe Venera on the venus surface (artist recreation).jpg",
        "credit": "wewewegrafikbaydeh (Reimund Bertrams)",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Space_probe_Venera_on_the_venus_surface_(artist_recreation).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.3,
          "end": 20.2,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 20.2,
          "end": 23.067,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.065,
      "end": 28.54,
      "text": "Mission control assumed the probe died instantly after landing on its side.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Venera 9 Space Probe 01.jpg",
        "credit": "Stolbovsky",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venera_9_Space_Probe_01.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.067,
          "end": 25.2,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 25.2,
          "end": 28.533,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.54,
      "end": 34.96,
      "text": "Weeks later, scientists found a faint twenty-three minute signal hidden beneath static on recorded tapes.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The Soviet Union 1988 CPA 6018 stamp (14th standard issue of Soviet Union. 1st issue. Setting up long-range space communications. Radio telescope) 1200dpi.jpg",
        "credit": "USSR Post (\u0440\u0438\u0441\u0443\u043d\u043e\u043a \u0412. \u042d. \u041a\u043e\u0432\u0430\u043b\u044f, \u0433\u0440\u0430\u0432\u044e\u0440\u0430 \u043d\u0430 \u043c\u0435\u0442\u0430\u043b\u043b\u0435 \u0413. \u0424. \u0417\u043e\u0442\u043e\u0432\u0430).",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Soviet_Union_1988_CPA_6018_stamp_(14th_standard_issue_of_Soviet_Union._1st_issue._Setting_up_long-range_space_communications._Radio_telescope)_1200dpi.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.533,
          "end": 34.967,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 34.96,
      "end": 41.355,
      "text": "The data confirmed a lead-melting surface temperature of four hundred seventy-five degrees Celsius.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Venus from Pioneer Venus in 1979.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venus_from_Pioneer_Venus_in_1979.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 34.967,
          "end": 41.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 41.355,
      "end": 44.907,
      "text": "Hidden data revealed a crashed space probe talking from Venus.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "1972 CPA 4166.jpg",
        "credit": "USSR Post",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1972_CPA_4166.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
